%% C4 Dynamic Diagram — the two loops.
%% A background task scrapes the engine; the arrival loop decides per request.
%% They are separate so the decision path never blocks on HTTP.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant W as Workload<br/>(generated or live traffic)
  participant R as AdmitPerf runner
  participant S as State cache
  participant P as Policy<br/>(e.g. kv_threshold)
  participant E as Engine adapter<br/>(vLLM)
  participant M as Results

  Note over R,E: The queue must form INSIDE the engine.<br/>A platform that serves one request at a time<br/>queues in front of it, and the signal stays flat.

  Note over R,E: Background loop, every scrape_interval_s
  R->>E: GET /metrics
  E-->>S: kv_used_fraction, num_requests_waiting,<br/>num_requests_running
  Note over S: stamped with its age on read

  Note over W,M: Arrival loop, per request
  W->>R: request due (tokens, SLO class, deadline)
  R->>S: read latest snapshot (no I/O)
  S-->>R: SystemState + age

  alt snapshot older than max_state_age_s
    R->>M: reject 503 "no_signal"
    Note over R: deciding on stale signal is guessing.<br/>A guess recorded as a decision corrupts the run.
  else snapshot usable
    R->>P: decide(request, state)
    P-->>R: ADMIT | DEFER(50ms) | REJECT("kv_pressure")
  end

  alt ADMIT
    R->>E: POST /v1/chat/completions (stream)
    E-->>R: tokens, timed on arrival
    R->>M: TTFT, inter-token gaps, deadline verdict
  else DEFER
    R->>R: sleep retry_after_ms
    R->>P: decide again, on fresher state
    Note over R: past max_defers it becomes a reject,<br/>so the request cannot vanish from the run.
  else REJECT
    R->>M: 429 / 503 / 529 with reason + the state it was decided on
  end
